{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q1439555","formula":"C₉H₁₉ClN₃O₅P","hill":"C9H19ClN3O5P","elements":["H","C","N","O","P","Cl"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":19.0,"N":3.0,"O":5.0,"P":1.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Fotemustine","ru":"Фотемустин","uk":"Фотемустин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fotemustine is a nitrosourea alkylating agent used in the treatment of metastatic melanoma. It is available in Europe but has not been approved by the United States FDA. A study has shown that fotemustine produces improved response rates but does not increase survival (over dacarbazine in the treatment of disseminated cutaneous melanoma. Median survival was 7.3 months with fotemustine versus 5.6 months with DTIC (P=.067).","ru":"Фотемустин — цитостатический противоопухолевый химиотерапевтический лекарственный препарат алкилирующего типа действия. Производное нитрозомочевины.","uk":"Фотемустин (англ. Fotemustine, лат. Fotemustinum) — синтетичний лікарський препарат, який за своєю хімічною структурою є похідним нітрозосечовини, та застосовується внутрішньовенно."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":104799,"mass":315.69,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCOP(=O)(C(C)NC(=O)N(CCCl)N=O)OCC","inchikey":"YAKWPXVTIGTRJH-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-(2-chloroethyl)-3-(1-diethoxyphosphorylethyl)-1-nitrosourea","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"104799","atoms":38,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-5.765,"y":0.563,"z":1.785,"el":"Cl"},{"x":2.305,"y":0.114,"z":-0.715,"el":"P"},{"x":3.8,"y":-0.324,"z":-0.277,"el":"O"},{"x":2.139,"y":1.535,"z":0.049,"el":"O"},{"x":2.083,"y":0.186,"z":-2.199,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.276,"y":-1.133,"z":1.571,"el":"O"},{"x":-3.598,"y":-0.043,"z":-2.25,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.139,"y":-0.754,"z":-0.394,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.495,"y":-0.588,"z":-0.323,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.476,"y":-0.242,"z":-1.774,"el":"N"},{"x":1.189,